{
  "title": "Colors, describing things, and adjective agreement",
  "note": "Adjectives usually follow the noun and agree with it in gender and number: el libro rojo, las casas rojas. Most adjectives ending in -e or a consonant change only for number: verde, verdes; azul, azules. Bueno and malo drop the -o before a masculine singular noun: un buen día.",
  "src": {
    "t": "Spanish 1A: Beginning Spanish (LibreTexts)",
    "u": "https://human.libretexts.org/Courses/Chabot_College/Spanish_1A%3A_Beginning_Spanish_(2026)"
